WEBVTT

00:00:00.013 --> 00:00:03.552
An empty pivot cell should not automatically become zero.

00:00:03.552 --> 00:00:07.152
NULL may mean no observation was recorded.

00:00:07.152 --> 00:00:11.887
Zero may mean the observation exists and its measured value is zero.

00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:13.922
Those are different facts.

00:00:13.922 --> 00:00:21.172
Before using ELSE zero or COALESCE, decide what an absent source row means for the analytical question.

00:00:21.172 --> 00:00:25.892
After reshaping, NULL and zero may have very different meanings.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:29.872
NULL can mean the category did not occur or was not measured;

00:00:29.872 --> 00:00:34.087
zero can mean it was measured and the value was truly zero.

00:00:34.087 --> 00:00:39.791
Do not replace NULL with zero unless that interpretation is correct for the business question.
